From: falconwing bring-up
Subject: [PATCH] Input: mxs-lradc-ts: don't look up IRQ index 0 as an IRQ number

The mxs-lradc MFD passes the touchscreen its interrupts as indices into
the LRADC node's DT "interrupts" (mapped with irq_of_parse_and_map()
here), and the touchscreen's own interrupt is index 0. Current kernels'
platform_get_irq_byname() warns that 0 is an invalid IRQ number and
fails, so the probe aborts and there is no touchscreen (seen on the
Chumby One). Read the resource directly instead.

---
diff -urN a/drivers/input/touchscreen/mxs-lradc-ts.c b/drivers/input/touchscreen/mxs-lradc-ts.c
--- a/drivers/input/touchscreen/mxs-lradc-ts.c	2026-10-08 21:35:37.869262739 -0700
+++ b/drivers/input/touchscreen/mxs-lradc-ts.c	2026-10-08 21:35:51.004654650 -0700
@@ -671,11 +671,22 @@
 	mxs_lradc_ts_hw_init(ts);
 
 	for (i = 0; i < 3; i++) {
-		irq = platform_get_irq_byname(pdev, mxs_lradc_ts_irq_names[i]);
-		if (irq < 0)
-			return irq;
+		/*
+		 * The MFD's IRQ resources are indices into the parent's DT
+		 * "interrupts", and the touchscreen's is index 0, which
+		 * platform_get_irq_byname() rejects as an invalid IRQ.
+		 */
+		struct resource *res =
+			platform_get_resource_byname(pdev, IORESOURCE_IRQ,
+						     mxs_lradc_ts_irq_names[i]);
+
+		if (!res)
+			return -ENXIO;
+		irq = res->start;
 
 		virq = irq_of_parse_and_map(node, irq);
+		if (!virq)
+			return -EINVAL;
 
 		mxs_lradc_ts_stop(ts);
 
